# 4. Database

### Definition

A database stores and manages application data.

### Why do we use it?

Applications need to permanently store information.

### Real life example

Instagram needs to store:

• Users
• Posts
• Comments
• Likes
• Followers

A database stores this information.

### Examples

**SQL databases**

MySQL
PostgreSQL
Oracle

**NoSQL databases**

MongoDB
Cassandra
DynamoDB

### Simple example

When you create an Instagram account:

```text
User ID: 101
Name: Ram
Email: ram@gmail.com
```

This information is stored in a database.

