# 5. Architecture

### Definition

Architecture describes **how different components of a system are organized and communicate with each other**.

### Why do we use it?

Large systems contain many components.

Architecture tells us how these components interact.

### Real life example

An online shopping system may have:

```text
User
  ↓
Frontend
  ↓
API Server
  ↓
Database
```

For a larger system:

```text
User
 ↓
Load Balancer
 ↓
Application Servers
 ↓
Cache
 ↓
Database
```

### Common architectures

Monolithic architecture

Microservices architecture

Layered architecture

Event driven architecture

