# 10. Protocols

### Definition

A protocol is a set of rules that defines how systems communicate.

### Why do we use them?

Different computers need common communication rules.

### Examples

HTTP

HTTPS

TCP

UDP

WebSocket

DNS

### Real life example

Imagine two people speaking English.

They understand each other because they follow a common language.

Similarly:

```text
Client
   ↕
HTTP
   ↕
Server
```

