# 14. Monitoring and Logging

## Monitoring

Monitoring means continuously observing the health and performance of the system.

## Logging

Logging means recording events that happen inside the system.

### Why do we use them?

To identify:

• Errors
• Slow requests
• Server failures
• High CPU usage
• Database problems
• Security issues

### Real life example

Suppose an application suddenly becomes slow.

Monitoring tells you:

```text
CPU: 95%
Memory: 90%
Response time: 8 seconds
```

Logs may tell you:

```text
Database connection timeout
```

Now engineers can investigate the problem.

### Common tools

Prometheus

Grafana

ELK

OpenTelemetry

